   "Our suggestion is to be deliberate about the next two roles rather than hurrying toward seniority. A full-time growth, partnerships or coordination seat at a young company would compound the founder instincts you already have, and education or health organizations would value exactly the record you hold: campaign ownership with a revenue result, multi-account discipline and steadiness with people under pressure. Keep the business running if you can; a founder line with numbers attached will out-argue most internships on any future application. And keep quantifying the way you already do, because half of total sales from one campaign is the kind of line hiring teams remember. If growth work in education specifically attracts you, an entry role at an education organization would put the sector's rhythms, terms and counterparties into the record early, and that compounds faster than any title.",
